  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The independent record shop",
    "overview": "Warm paper, compact sans-serif controls and generous serif headlines frame a small collection of original music artwork. The site feels editorial and tactile: thin dividers organize the page, raspberry identifies actions, and olive provides a distinct working surface for the brief composer.\n\nThis is a scan of the implemented website, not a product-wide identity specification. It covers the landing page, brief composer and explicit Starlight overrides. It does not govern the MCP App. The north-star phrase and atmosphere language are descriptive and provisional. The unattended implementation did not establish a user-selected comp or a public seed reference; the later direction roll does not replace that missing pre-implementation workshop. Documentation records observed design, not whole-surface ship approval. See [the website brief](docs/design/site-brief.md) for the process record.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream paper and dark ink support long reading; raspberry distinguishes actions.",
      "Fraunces supplies headings and the composed brief; DM Sans supplies prose and controls.",
      "Flat interface surfaces use thin dividers and tonal changes, while imagery carries physical texture.",
      "The brief remains selectable, wraps naturally and grows with its content on narrow screens."
